  "text": "Skip to content\nNino Chavez\nWork\nSessions\nLearn\nWriting\nPhotography\nAbout\nSearch site\nABOUT\nNOW\nLINKS\nABOUT\nCHICAGO\nBUILDING SINCE 1999\nNino\nChavez\n\nI’m a product architect in Chicago. I’ve spent more than 25 years turning complicated decisions into working software.\n\n01 / BIOGRAPHY\nThe short version\n\nI started in software engineering, moved through architecture and consulting, and now work as a Product Architect at commerce.com. I still prefer the part where a decision becomes a working system.\n\nOutside the day job, I run Let’s Pepper, build and operate Rally HQ, shoot volleyball through Flickday Media, publish Signal Dispatch, and keep a music practice on SoundCloud. They look different, but each has to work for the people in front of it.\n\nThe practice has a newer shape too: I take engagements outside my own domain and come back in days with working software, evidence a client can check, and problems they couldn’t see. AI agents supply the depth; the architecture years supply the steering. I wrote about the first full test of that model in The Depth Penalty Is Gone.\n\nCURRENT ROLE\nProduct Architect\nORGANIZATION\ncommerce.com\nHOME\nChicago\nSOFTWARE PRACTICE\nSince 1999\n02 / THROUGHLINE\nWhat connects the work\n\nThe form changes. Each practice asks me to make something useful, run it under real conditions, and own the result.\n\n01\nArchitecture\nHold the shape of a system while decisions become working software.\nOPEN THE WORK →\n02\nLive operations\nRun registration, schedules, brackets, scoring, and the event around them.\nSEE VOLLEYBALL WORK →\n03\nPhotography\nAnticipate the point before it happens, then make the result easy to find and keep.\nOPEN PHOTOGRAPHY →\n04\nWriting\nTurn working evidence and unfinished thinking into published arguments.\nREAD SIGNAL DISPATCH →\n05\nMusic\nSelect and sequence records for the room.\nLISTEN ON SOUNDCLOUD\n↗\n(OPENS IN A NEW TAB)\n03 / WORKING MODEL\nHow I work with agents\n\nAgents help me research, draft, code, test, review, and package more work than I could handle alone.\n\nI still decide what the work is for, what can be published, and whether the evidence supports the claim.\n\nSee the method in Blueprint →\nSee the sessions →\nWHERE TO GO NEXT\nChoose the context you need\nNow\nA dated view of active work and current attention.\n→\nLinks\nMaintained destinations for sites, profiles, music, and contact.\n→\nWork\nProducts, tools, methods, operations, and collections.\n→\nELSEWHERE\nLINKEDIN ↗\n(OPENS IN A NEW TAB)\nGITHUB ↗\n(OPENS IN A NEW TAB)\nSOUNDCLOUD ↗\n(OPENS IN A NEW TAB)\nEMAIL ↗\n\nNino Chavez\n\nProduct architect and builder in Chicago.\n\nWork\nSessions\nLearn\nWriting\nPhotography\nAbout\nNow\nLinks\nPrivacy\nGitHub ↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn ↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nEmail ↗",
